+# Queue retry policy
+
+Runtime: Linux backend service. This policy is framework-neutral.
+
+```json
+{
+  "maxAttempts": 3,
+  "retryStatus": [408, 429, 500, 502, 503],
+  "preserveJobId": true
+}
+```
+
+- `maxAttempts` counts the initial execution and all retries: at most three executions per job (one initial attempt and up to two retries).
+- Retry a failed attempt only when its status is in `retryStatus` and fewer than three attempts have run. The allowlist identifies the transient statuses covered by this policy; unlisted statuses and failures without a status are not retried automatically.
+- Authentication and authorization failures, including 401 and 403, terminate without retry.
+- Success terminates processing without retry. A retryable failure on the third attempt terminates as exhausted; it must not schedule a fourth attempt.
+- Keep the original job ID for every attempt. Retry scheduling must not create a new logical job or reset its attempt count. Persist the attempt count across rescheduling and worker restarts so that the limit remains effective.
